 "upload": {
  "title": "Israel Election: Exit Polls Split, No Majority #shorts",
  "description": "Israel's election on October 27, 2026 produced no clear winner in exit polls. Channel 12 first showed Gadi Eisenkot's bloc ahead 52 to 50, then a revised poll showed Benjamin Netanyahu's bloc ahead 52 to 49; Kan showed a tie (reports via CNN, Axios and others). Likud is projected near 27 seats and Eisenkot's Yashar about 21 in the 120-seat Knesset, but neither bloc reaches the 61 needed. Arab parties are projected at 16 to 19 seats; Netanyahu's side rules out working with them and Eisenkot has all but ruled it out, per reports. Both leaders claimed victory. Exit polls are not official results; the Central Elections Committee count continues. Axios says Netanyahu would likely remain caretaker prime minister.\n\nSources:\nCNN: Israeli election results: No clear winner as exit polls suggest rebuke for Netanyahu (Oct 27, 2026)\nAxios: Netanyahu, Eisenkot blocs running close, but both shy of majority (Oct 27, 2026)\nNBC News: Exit polls indicate no clear winner in Israeli election (Oct 27, 2026)\nThe Jerusalem Post: Netanyahu, Eisenkot both fail to win majority in exit polls (Oct 27, 2026)\ni24NEWS: Exit poll (Oct 27, 2026)\nYnet News: Revised exit polls (Oct 27-28, 2026)\n\n#geopolitics #Israel #Netanyahu #election",
